# Polytetrafluoroethylene, phase IV (15/7 helix): E. S. Clark & L. T. Muus, Z. Kristallogr. 117, 119 (1962), doi:10.1524/zkri.1962.117.2-3.119
# space group P31 (c the chain axis) (No. 144), Z = 15 CF2 per cell; hexagonal cell (25 C) p. 121; 15/7 helix packed in P31, one chain per cell, p. 127; no atomic coordinates in the paper
# coordinates: generated from the helix symmetry and the cited lattice (tools/make_polymer_crystals.py), not refined
# correction / model: no atomic coordinates in the paper: the chain is generated from the 15/7 helix and the cited lattice, not refined: 15 CF2 in 7 turns span c exactly (rise 1.3000 A, twist 168.00 deg per CF2), C-C 1.54 A, C-F 1.34 A, F-C-F 108 deg (Hasegawa, Takahashi, Chatani & Tadokoro, Polym. J. 3, 600 (1972), p. 603); this gives C-C-C 115.56 deg, carbon helix radius 0.415 A and fluorine radius 1.618 A (Bunn & Howells, Nature 174, 549 (1954): 116 deg, about 0.42 A and 1.64 +- 0.05 A); one chain on the cell axis, setting angle 6 deg (the paper gives none: the one with the longest shortest F...F between chains, 2.802 A)
# correction / model: at this setting angle the chain's own twofold axes fall on the lattice's, so the cell also has them: P3112 (No. 151, origin at z = 11/30), which contains the paper's P31
# hydrogens: none (perfluorinated chain)
# written in P1 with every atom of the paper's cell; 2.3024 g/cm3, shortest contacts beyond 1-3: H...H none below 3.2 A, H...X none below 3.2 A, X...X 2.60 A
